==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|vpright||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|upright}}, {{m|enm|uppryght}}, {{m|enm|upriht}}, from {{inh|en|ang|upriht||t=upright; erect}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*upprehtaz}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|up|right}}. Cognate with {{cog|stq|apgjucht|t=upright}}, {{cog|fy|oprjocht|t=upright}}, {{cog|nl|oprecht|t=upright}}, {{cog|nds-de|uprecht|t=upright}}, {{cog|de|aufrecht|t=upright}}, {{cog|sv|upprätt|t=upright}}, {{cog|is|uppréttur|t=upright}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈʌpɹaɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-upright.ogg|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[vertical|Vertical]]; [[erect]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1608|author=William Shakespeare|title=The merry Deuill of Edmonton|section=introduction, [http://books.google.co.uk/books?id=OSLPAAAAMAAJ&pg=PT7&dq=%22stiffned+haire+stands+vpright%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=0ED3TtO1Bcev8gOd5IHXAQ&ved=0CE8Q6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=%22stiffned%20haire%20stands%20vpright%22&f=false lines 1-4]
|passage=''Fab''[''ell'']'':'' What meanes the tolling of this fatall chime, // O what a trembling horror ſtrikes my hart! // My ſtiffned haire ſtands '''vpright''' on my head, // As doe the briſtles of a porcupine.}}
# In its proper orientation; not [[overturned]].
#: {{ux|en|My brother didn't get angry when his son knocked over the lamp; he simply called the boy over and helped him set it '''upright''' again.}}
# Greater in [[height]] than [[breadth]].
# {{senseid|en|moral ethical}} {{lb|en|figuratively|ethics}} Of good [[moral]]s; reliable and trustworthy; practicing [[ethical]] values.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Job|1|1|text=There was a man in the land of Uz, whose name was Job; and that man was perfect and '''upright''', and one that feared God, and eschewed evil.}}
# {{lb|en|golf|of a golf club}} Having a [[head]] at approximately a [[right angle]] with the [[shaft]].
# Characterized by a style of running with the head and shoulders held high.
#: {{cot|en|downhill}}
#: {{ux|en|He's an '''upright''' runner.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|vertical, erect}} {{l|en|orthograde}}, {{l|en|surrect}} {{qualifier|obsolete, rare}}

