===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any [[vertical]] part of a [[structure]], especially a part that provides [[support]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1942|author=Reuben Swinburne Clymer|title=The Philosophy of Fire|page=64
|passage=On the change in architectural forms from the pyramidal to the obeliscar, the fires were transferred from the altars, or cubes, to the summits of the typical '''uprights''', or towers; {{...}}}}
## {{lb|en|soccer}} A [[goal post]].
## {{lb|en|American football}} The poles of a field goal post.
## {{lb|en|slang}} A [[leg]].
## {{lb|en|camping}} A [[tentpole]] that holds aloft the center or sides of a [[tent]].
##: {{coo|en|ridge}}
# ''Something characterized by verticality.''
## The state of being vertical or perpendicular.
##: {{ux|en|Can you fix that? It's out of '''upright'''.}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} Characterized by being awake and out of bed.
##: {{syn|en|up}}
## A word clued by the successive initial, middle, or final letters of the [[cross-light]]s in a [[double acrostic]] or [[triple acrostic]].
##: {{holo|en|double acrostic|triple acrostic}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{short for|en|upright bass}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{short for|en|upright bicycle}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{short for|en|upright freezer}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{short for|en|upright piano}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{short for|en|upright [[arcade game]] [[cabinet]]}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Jon Peddie|title=The History of Visual Magic in Computers|page=181
|passage=The video arcade machines are typically in stand up arcade cabinets, although some have been built as tables. The '''uprights''' have a monitor and controls in front and players insert coins or tokens into the machines to play the game.}}
## {{ellipsis of|en|upright [[vacuum cleaner]]}}.
## {{lb|en|obsolete|hunting|dialect|British}} The tips of the antlers of a young deer.

